==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Power Piledriver Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Neo Piledriver Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Piledriver Cat's consecutive Omni Strikes and guaranteed [[Knockback]]s sound decent at first glance. However, there lies many weaknesses. The area covered is not very large, plus, her [[Omni Strike]] is only meant to hit Zombies behind her, but her subsequent multi-hits lack the forward piercing range to consecutively reach Zombies knocked back by her previous multi-hits—most of the time, Piledriver won't have all her multi-hits hit the same enemy unless the enemy stays close enough. Between that, her slow attack rate, foreswing animation and recharge time, it's just better to rely on [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight Cat]]. What you will be using Piledriver Cat for can be done by Ectoweight with more spammability (for example, to counter [[Big Sal]] or [[Miss Haka]]), although Piledriver still has the advantages of area attacks, more range and guaranteed knockbacks from consecutive multi-hits. Even putting Ectoweight aside, there are a couple other alternatives that outclass Piledriver, making her subpar if you have any of those aforementioned units.

